          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q6-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Consider 6 as the hypotenuse, or 5 and 6 as the two shorter sides.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "If 6 is the hypotenuse:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+5^2&=6^2\\\\x^2&=36-25\\\\x&=\\sqrt{11}\\end{align*}$$\nIf 5 and 6 are the two shorter sides:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=5^2+6^2\\\\x^2&=61\\\\x&=\\sqrt{61}\\end{align*}$$\nThe side of length 5 cannot be the hypotenuse because 6 is longer. The two possible lengths are $\\sqrt{11}$ and $\\sqrt{61}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
